figure='''<h2>Animal cell: simple grayscale schematic</h2><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 700 300" role="img" aria-label="Animal cell schematic: a membrane encloses a DNA-containing nucleus and several mitochondria; not to scale."><ellipse cx="300" cy="150" rx="260" ry="125" fill="white" stroke="#222" stroke-width="4"/><circle cx="230" cy="135" r="60" fill="#eee" stroke="#222" stroke-width="3"/><text x="195" y="130" font-size="20">Nucleus</text><text x="209" y="155" font-size="18">DNA</text><g fill="#ddd" stroke="#222" stroke-width="3"><ellipse cx="395" cy="90" rx="42" ry="20"/><ellipse cx="390" cy="208" rx="42" ry="20"/></g><path d="M361 90l12-9 12 18 12-18 12 9M355 208l12-9 12 18 12-18 12 9" stroke="#222" fill="none" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M436 88L520 60M500 220L575 245" stroke="#222" stroke-width="2"/><text x="520" y="53" font-size="20">Mitochondria</text><text x="490" y="271" font-size="20">Cell membrane</text></svg><p>Text equivalent: A cell membrane encloses the animal cell. Inside are a nucleus containing DNA and several mitochondria. Scale, shape and positions are illustrative. The reference explains the function of each structure.</p>'''
